    "High" : {
      "comment" : "Visual representation of a reference range (e.g. \"Normal\" range) shown as a shaded band on a sparkline.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "HRV measures the tiny variation in time between each heartbeat. Counterintuitively, **more variation is better** — it means your nervous system is flexible and recovering well. A higher HRV typically signals good sleep, low stress, and solid fitness. A low or falling HRV often appears before you feel run-down. HRV is highly personal, so trends over time matter more than any single number." : {
      "comment" : "An explanation of what HRV is and why it's important.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
